  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 130 PM MDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nBy Sunday and Monday, the monsoon high will expand to near 598dm and \nbecome centered more over northeast NM and west TX. This will drive \nthe main moisture plume west of the Cont Divide. Steering flow will \nalso become more southeast/northwest with less convection expected \nover central and eastern NM. Max temps will also rise into the upper \n90s and low 100s for parts of the RGV and eastern NM so additional \nheat risk impacts are expected.\n\nThe rest of the week will be typical of late July with the monsoon \nhigh center drifting west into the Four Corners region. Abundant \nmoisture beneath the high will allow for daily rounds of showers and \nstorms to develop over the high terrain then move erratically into \nnearby lowlands thru the afternoon. Max temps will stay above normal \nnext week, especially for eastern NM.",
